node_modules

# `**` matters: .dockerignore follows Go's filepath.Match, where `*` does not cross a `/`. Written as
# `*.test.ts` this excluded nothing at all — every suite in src/ was being copied into the published
# image, where it is dead weight that also imports a browser driver the runtime image does not have.
**/*.test.ts

# The build's output, not its input. The image builds the page itself in its own stage; copying a dist/
# from the developer's machine would ship whatever they last happened to build.
ui/dist

# The screenshot harness. Not copied by any COPY either, but stated here so that adding a `COPY . .`
# one day does not quietly publish a page that renders fixtures instead of the machine's real state.
preview
